// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DPM SPDX license list resource.
//
// Embeds spdx-licenses.txt as DPM_SPDX_LICENSES / RCDATA so every dpm.exe,
// DPM.IDE.*.dll and DSpecCreator binary carries the full SPDX license list
// (one "id=name,url" line per license). Used to decide whether a license
// string is a known SPDX id (and so should be rendered as a clickable link)
// and to populate license pick lists.
//
// Linked by DPM.Core.Utils.Spdx via a `{$R}` directive - see that unit for
// the resource name and type the loader expects (DPM_SPDX_LICENSES, RCDATA).
//
// The first line of spdx-licenses.txt is 'SPDXLicenseListVersion=<release>' - the published
// SPDX license list release the file was generated from. DPM.Core.Utils.Spdx lifts it out
// of the list and SPDX documents declare it as creationInfo.licenseListVersion.
//
// Update flow:
//   1. Regenerate spdx-licenses.txt (ids + names + urls) from a published SPDX license list
//      release, keeping the version header, CRLF line endings and the ANSI/CP1252 encoding
//      the loader expects.
//   2. Recompile the resource BY HAND:  brcc32 DPM.Spdx.rc -foDPM.Spdx.res
//      Nothing does this for you - DPM.Spdx.RES is a checked-in binary and no .dproj lists
//      this .rc, so an msbuild (or IDE) build just links whatever .res is already on disk.
//      Editing the .txt alone leaves the previous license list silently embedded.
//   3. Commit the regenerated DPM.Spdx.RES alongside spdx-licenses.txt, then ship.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DPM_SPDX_LICENSES RCDATA "spdx-licenses.txt"
